From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:38:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nb/intel/haswell: Reserve the ECAM window as a motherboard
 resource

The MCFG table points the OS to the ECAM window at
CONFIG_ECAM_MMCONF_BASE_ADDRESS, but no PNP0C02 device listed it: PDRC
has the RCBA, MCH, DMI and EP BARs, TXT, the TPM, the ICH range, eDRAM
and GDXC. The PCI Firmware Specification (3.3, 4.1.2) asks for the
window to be reserved as a motherboard resource, and that is where
Linux looks for it when it checks the window after the ACPI interpreter
is up (pci_mmcfg_reserved(), "ECAM ... not reserved in ACPI motherboard
resources" otherwise).

Add it to PDRC, after the other fixed ranges. The window stays out of
the host bridge's _CRS, which lists the MMIO below and above it.

TEST=The DSDT of the W541 builds (mrc and nri) of ouroBIOS compiles
with iasl -w3 without a new warning. Still to test on the W541:
/proc/iomem shows the window under the pnp device of PDRC, and the
boot of Linux, Windows and macOS as before.
---
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/acpi/hostbridge.asl | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/acpi/hostbridge.asl b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/acpi/hostbridge.asl
index 983190c1ee..e11e16478c 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/acpi/hostbridge.asl
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/acpi/hostbridge.asl
@@ -231,6 +231,9 @@ Device (PDRC)
 		Memory32Fixed (ReadWrite, 0xfed45000, 0x0004b000) // Misc ICH
 		Memory32Fixed (ReadWrite, EDRAM_BASE_ADDRESS, EDRAM_BASE_SIZE)
 		Memory32Fixed (ReadWrite, GDXC_BASE_ADDRESS, GDXC_BASE_SIZE)
+		/* ECAM, which the MCFG table points to (PCI Firmware 3.3, 4.1.2) */
+		Memory32Fixed (ReadWrite, CONFIG_ECAM_MMCONF_BASE_ADDRESS,
+			       CONFIG_ECAM_MMCONF_LENGTH)
 	})
 
 	// Current Resource Settings
